{"conversation":"Oh okay, so I should think like recipes are like courses and ingredients are like prerequisites; I can only "take a course" or make a recipe if I have all the prerequisite ingredients or supplies. I guess I need to track which ingredients are already available and then try making recipes one by one if their ingredients are all ready. I think this is similar to a kind of BFS or maybe topological sort? Hmm, I will try to build a set of supplies first and then maybe loop through recipes to check if I can make them.","python_code":"class Solution:
    def findAllRecipes(self, recipes: List[str], ingredients: List[List[str]], supplies: List[str]) -> List[str]:
        available = set(supplies)
        res = []
        for i in range(len(recipes)):
            can_make = True
            for ing in ingredients[i]:
                if ing not in available:
                    can_make = False
                    break
            if can_make:
                res.append(recipes[i])
        return res"}

{"conversation":"Hmm, I think right now my code only checks the initial supplies and doesn't update available ingredients with new recipes made during the iteration. So if a recipe depends on another recipe as ingredient, my code will not recognize it unless it's in initial supplies. So I guess I need to repeatedly try making recipes and update the supplies until I can't make any more new recipes. Maybe a while loop that tries to add new recipes to available?","python_code":"class Solution:
    def findAllRecipes(self, recipes: List[str], ingredients: List[List[str]], supplies: List[str]) -> List[str]:
        available = set(supplies)
        res = []
        n = len(recipes)
        made = set()
        changed = True
        while changed:
            changed = False
            for i in range(n):
                if recipes[i] not in made:
                    can_make = True
                    for ing in ingredients[i]:
                        if ing not in available:
                            can_make = False
                            break
                    if can_make:
                        res.append(recipes[i])
                        made.add(recipes[i])
                        available.add(recipes[i])
                        changed = True
        return res"}

